Spencer is a 2021 historical psychological drama film directed
by Pablo Larraín and written by Steven Knight.

11
01:00:45,714 --> 01:00:51,714
The film is about Diana, Princess of Wales's existential crisis during the Christmas of 1991,
as she considers divorcing Prince Charles and leaving the British royal family.

12
01:06:17,142 --> 01:06:23,142
Kristen Stewart and Jack Farthing star as Diana and Charles respectively, along with Jack
Neilen and Freddie Spry as Prince William and Prince Harry, respectively.

13
01:11:48,571 --> 01:11:54,571
Also starring Timothy Spall, Sean Harris, and Sally Hawkins.

14
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:26,000
It is the second film in Larraín's trilogy of iconic 20th century
women, succeeding Jackie (2016) and preceding Maria (2024).

15
01:22:51,428 --> 01:22:57,428
Spencer premiered at the 78th Venice International Film Festival on 3 September 2021, and was
theatrically released in the United Kingdom and the United States on 5 November 2021.

16
01:28:22,857 --> 01:28:28,857
The film grossed $25.2 million worldwide on an $18 million budget.

17
01:33:54,285 --> 01:34:00,285
It received generally positive reviews from critics, with
Stewart's performance garnering widespread praise.

18
01:39:25,714 --> 01:39:31,714
For her performance as Diana, Stewart was nominated for the Academy Award for Best
Actress, as well as a Golden Globe Award and a Critics' Choice Movie Award.

19
01:44:57,142 --> 01:45:03,142
The film explores themes of princess, marriage crisis,
royal family, biography, based on true story.

